  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of the variance of first <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> positive integral multiples of <math><mn>4</mn></math> to the variance of first <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> positive odd numbers is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the variance of first <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> natural numbers is <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> then the variance of first <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> integral multiple of <math><mn>4</mn></math> is <math><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />and the variance of first <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math> odd natural numbers is <math><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Then, the required ratio is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
